   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve y^2 = x^3 - 12x + 11, for which dy/dx = (3x^2 - 12)/(2y). Every point on the curve at which the tangent line is horizontal has the same x-coordinate. What is that x-coordinate?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Negate",
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A horizontal tangent needs the numerator to vanish: 3x^2 - 12 = 0, so x = 2 or x = -2.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute x = 2 into the curve: y^2 = 8 - 24 + 11 = -5, which has no real solution, so no point of the curve has x = 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            5
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute x = -2: y^2 = -8 + 24 + 11 = 27, so y = 3 sqrt(3) or y = -3 sqrt(3), and 2y is not zero at either point.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The only x-coordinate at which the tangent is horizontal is x = -2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            2
         ]
      }
   ],
